course: dictionary
lesson: 11650
title: Made by people, not nature
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you where something came from. Artificially is one of them: it means made or done by people, not by nature. «The sweets were artificially coloured, so they glowed bright pink.» Nature did not make that pink. A factory did.
explain: The word can also mean not real or natural, or forced. «The shop kept the price of milk artificially low.» The price was not left to change by itself. Someone pushed it down on purpose.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Words like colour, sweetened, grown in a lab, or made in a factory often point to artificial. Then check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word. If it still makes sense, you have it.
fact: Artificially means made or done by people, not by nature.
fact: «Artificially» can also mean not real or natural, or forced.
fact: «Artificially» comes from the word artificial, and it is an adverb: it tells you how something was done.
fact: «The scientists artificially grew the crystals in a tank.» Crystals grown in a lab were made by people, not found in nature.
fact: «Artificially» is often used on food labels, such as «artificially sweetened» or «artificially coloured».
exercise: «The sweets were artificially coloured.» What does artificially mean here? | Given away free | Very sweet to taste | Coloured by the sun | *Made or coloured by people, not by nature
exercise: «The crystals were artificially grown in the science lab.» Find and copy the word that tells you people made them. | *artificially | science | lab | crystals
exercise: «The shop kept the price of milk artificially low.» What does artificially suggest about the price? | *It was forced to stay low, not left to change naturally | It was set by nature, like the weather | It was given away for free | It was very high
test: «This drink was artificially sweetened, not sweetened by ripe fruit.» What does artificially mean? | Sweet because it is ripe fruit | Sold in a big bottle | *Made sweet by people, not by nature | Very cold
test: Which word means about the same as artificially in the sense of made by people? | Naturally | *Man-made | Ancient | Wild
exam: Which sentence uses artificially correctly? | The clouds artificially sent the rain to the hills | The tree artificially grew tall in the forest | The river artificially ran down to the sea | *The scientists artificially grew the crystals in a tank
